{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And He said: I will hide My face from them.</b> I have already mentioned in the section of Bereshit that 'saying' with regard to HaShem means will or thought, and the expression 'I will hide My face' — I will hide the ה which is My face, and this is clear." "<b>Children in whom is no faithfulness.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): אמון is a noun of attribute, and the sense is to say that there is no trustworthy man among them." "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> בנים לא אמון בם — that is, they do not answer Amen, and it is spelled without a וי״ו, and from here is a hint to the greatness of the power of the one who answers Amen, that he is greater than the one who blesses." "<b>And by way of the Kabbalah:</b> בנים לא אמון בם — they have no artisan and nurturer, for the force called פנים is the artisan and nurturer of the children, and since they are in the hiding of the face, behold, the artisan has departed, he is gone, he is not within them; and this artisan is the final ה of the Name, and this is אסתירה פני מהם, and I have already mentioned it."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:53:16.676308146Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}